Maintainer: Yannick Chabanois <contact@openmptcprouter.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), clang, llvm, libbpf-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: mptcp-bpf-overflow
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, libbpf0 | libbpf1
Recommends: mptcp-weight-manager
Description: MPTCP BPF Overflow Scheduler
 BPF MPTCP scheduler that uses the subflows by weight: a lower-weight
 subflow carries data only while every higher-weight one has a full
 congestion window, and only when that makes the data complete sooner.
 Subflows of the same weight are shared as by ECF.
 .
 The weights are those of mptcp-bpf-weight, read from the same pinned
 BPF maps and set with mptcp-weight-manager. On this (server/VPS) side
 they are keyed by the MPTCP endpoint id the router assigned to each
 WAN, and the router syncs them.
 .
 The compiled BPF object is installed into /usr/share/bpf/scheduler/
 and can be loaded with mptcpd or iproute2.
